{"records":[{"id":"dyy8xfvpkf","title":"Metamorphic proteins at the basis of human autophagy initiation and lipid transfer. Nguyen et al.","description":"Autophagy is a conserved intracellular degradation pathway that generates de novo double-membrane autophagosomes to target a wide range of material for lysosomal degradation. In multicellular organisms, autophagy initiation requires the timely assembly of a contact site between the ER and the nascent autophagosome. Here, we report the in vitro reconstitution of a full-length seven-subunit human autophagy initiation super-complex, build on a core complex of ATG13-101 and ATG9. Assembly of this core complex requires the rare ability of ATG13 and ATG101 to switch between distinct folds. The slow spontaneous metamorphic conversion is rate-limiting for the self-assembly of the super-complex. The interaction of the core complex with ATG2-WIPI4 enhances tethering of membrane vesicles and accelerates lipid transfer of ATG2 by both ATG9 and ATG13-101. Our work uncovers the molecular basis of the contact site and its assembly mechanisms imposed by the metamorphosis of ATG13-101 to regulate autophagosome biogenesis in space and time.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-04-19T12:41:37.734Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dyy8xfvpkf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/dyy8xfvpkf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alex","last_name":"Faesen","orcid":"0000-0002-4685-1463"},{"first_name":"Björn","last_name":"Stork","orcid":"0000-0002-4167-7806"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Autophagy","Reconstitution Experiment"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4gmsw3t82z","title":"Optimized protocols for RNA-induced silencing complex assembly and cleavage assays","description":"siRNAs and miRNAs guide the RNA-induced silencing complex (RISC) to regulate the expression of their target mRNA. In vitro RISC assembly and cleavage assays are proven helpful tools to characterize the biochemical properties of the RISC. Here, we provide an optimized protocol for RISC assembly and cleavage in vitro without the use of radiolabeled RNA. This protocol can directly detect RISC assembly and cleavage products within 5 days. Moreover, the methods presented here can simultaneously detect 5′- and 3′-cleavage products.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-04-27T20:18:00.168Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4gmsw3t82z","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4gmsw3t82z"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Gao","last_name":"Yajie","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ynrr4j7t4s","title":"Membrane phosphoinositides regulate GPCR-beta-arrestin complex assembly and dynamics","description":"Source data for Janetzko et al. 2022 Cell. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2022.10.018","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-11-10T21:46:40.225Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ynrr4j7t4s","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ynrr4j7t4s"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"John","last_name":"Janetzko","orcid":"0000-0003-1604-2515"},{"first_name":"Brian ","last_name":"Kobilka","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Asuka","last_name":"Inoue","orcid":"0000-0003-0805-4049"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Signaling","Luminescence","Protein-Protein Interaction","Fluorescence","Surface Plasmon Resonance","Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8zsg9hhr6n","title":"EMC3 regulates mesenchymal cell survival via control of the mitotic spindle assembly","description":"Eukaryotic cells transit through the cell cycle to produce two daughter cells. Dysregulation of the cell cycle leads to cell death or tumorigenesis. Herein, we found that a subunit of the Endoplasmic Reticulum (ER) membrane complex, EMC3, is a key regulator of the cell cycle. Conditional deletion of Emc3 in mouse embryonic mesoderm led to reduced size and patterning defects of multiple organs. Emc3 deficiency impaired cell proliferation, causing spindle assembly defects, chromosome mis-segregation, cell cycle arrest at G2/M, and apoptosis. Upon entry into mitosis, mesenchymal cells upregulate EMC3 protein levels and localize EMC3 to the mitotic centrosomes. Further analysis indicated that EMC3 interacts with VCP and Aurora A in mitotic cells. EMC3 works together with VCP to tightly regulate the levels and activity of Aurora A, an essential factor for centrosome function and mitotic spindle assembly: while over-expression of EMC3 or VCP degraded Aurora A, loss of EMC3 or VCP led to increased stability but the reduced activity of Aurora A in mitosis. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-24T17:11:13.847Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8zsg9hhr6n","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8zsg9hhr6n"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jeffrey","last_name":"Whitsett","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fj6xn2hsb7","title":"Effect of increasing valine level in the diet on performance, egg quality and serum components in laying quails","description":"One of the branched-chain amino acids, valine, is regarded as fifty limiting amino acid for birds fed with based on corn-soybean meal. It also plays a crucial role in performance, protein and lipid metabolism, energy stability, cell function and immunity. Increasing valine level decreased egg weight and egg mass. At the same time, the albumen index and the Haugh unit decreased. Serum glucose and triglyceride levels reduced with increasing valine level. Additionally, it decreased erythrocyte and haematocrit, but increased white blood cell, neutrophil and lymphocyte counts.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-08T11:52:05.011Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fj6xn2hsb7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fj6xn2hsb7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Osman","last_name":"OLGUN","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Poultry Nutrition"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"dpmdwgkppj","title":"Assembly of the WHIP-TRIM14-PPP6C Mitochondrial Complex Promotes RIG-I-mediated Antiviral Signaling . Peng Tan et al.","description":"Raw image for \"Assembly of the WHIP-TRIM14-PPP6C Mitochondrial Complex Promotes RIG-I-mediated Antiviral Signaling\",  revision manuscript  MOLECULAR-CELL-D-17-00107","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2017-11-02T19:21:04.954Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dpmdwgkppj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/dpmdwgkppj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rongfu","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Confocal Microscopy","Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vtk57cgv43","title":"A negative regulator of mitochondrial complex I assembly adapts respiration to cellular energy demand. Zhirong Li et al.","description":"This folder contains the original images for the submitted manuscript \"A negative regulator of mitochondrial complex I assembly adapts respiration to cellular energy demand\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-23T20:33:02.748Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vtk57cgv43","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vtk57cgv43"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Chao","last_name":"Tong","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grant_id":"92157201, 92254305, 32030027, 91754103"},{"id":"https://ror.org/05yj3y977","name":"Science and Technology Department of Zhejiang Province","grant_id":"LZ23C070002"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grant_id":"32570807"}],"categories":["Confocal Microscopy","Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f9kkszrtch","title":"Growth Optimized Aminoacyl-tRNA Synthetase Levels Prevent Maximal tRNA Charging. Parker et al","description":"tRNA charging Northern blot to demonstrate increased charging of tRNA with cognate aaRS overproduction.\n\nOne .tif file of multiple blots imaged together. Intensity was changed in figure to aid viewing.\n\nIn order from left to right:\nProbed for argACG tRNA:\nLane 1 - Deacylated control sample\nLane 2 - WT 168 sample\nLane 3 - ArgS overproduction sample\nLane 4 - ArgS overproduction sample Replicate \nLane 5 - SerS overproduction sample\n\nProbed for serGCU tRNA:\nLane 1 - Deacylated control sample\nLane 2 - WT 168 sample\nLane 3 - SerS overproduction sample\nLane 4 - IleS overproduction sample\n\nProbed for ileCAU tRNA:\nLane 1 - Deacylated control sample\nLane 2 - WT 168 sample\nLane 3 - IleS overproduction sample\nLane 4 - LeuS overproduction sample\n\nProbed for leuUAA tRNA:\nLane 1 - Deacylated control sample\nLane 2 - WT 168 sample\nLane 3 - LeuS overproduction sample\nLane 4 - IleS overproduction sample","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-07-16T15:33:02.428Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f9kkszrtch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f9kkszrtch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Gene-Wei","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Biological Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vv3pvnb75h","title":"Figure 1D - tRNA acylation levels of exponentially growing MG1655 and MG1655relA::HTF measured by Northern blotting analysis","description":"tRNA acylation levels of exponentially growing MG1655 and MG1655relA::HTF measured by northern blotting analysis. Total tRNA was extracted from cells growing in MOPS minimal medium with 0.2% glucose as the carbon source before and after isoleucine starvation. A fraction of the purified tRNA was deacylated (by 100 mM Tris-HCL [pH 9]) and charged and uncharged samples were separated by urea PAGE and transferred to a membrane. tRNAileTUV, tRNAasnUTVW and tRNAtrpT were detected by hybridization with radiolabeled tRNA-specific DNA oligonucleotide probes.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-04-04T13:45:53.451Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vv3pvnb75h","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vv3pvnb75h"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kenn","last_name":"Gerdes","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Southern Blot Analysis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3sdsc83vsn","title":"Genome-Scale Exon Perturbation Screens Uncover Exons Critical for Cell Fitness","description":"CRISPR-Cas technology has transformed functional genomics, yet understanding how individual exons differentially shape cellular phenotypes remains limited. Here, we optimized and conducted massively parallel exon deletion and splice site mutation screens in human cell lines to identify exons that regulate cellular fitness. Fitness-promoting exons are prevalent in essential and highly expressed genes, and commonly overlap with protein domains and interaction interfaces. Conversely, fitness-suppressing exons are enriched in non-essential genes, exhibiting lower inclusion levels, and overlap with intrinsically disordered regions and disease-associated mutations. In-depth mechanistic investigation of the TAF5 alternative exon-8, screen hit, revealed that its inclusion is required for assembly of the TFIID general transcription initiation complex, thereby regulating global gene expression output. Collectively, our orthogonal exon perturbation screens established a comprehensive repository of phenotypically important exons and uncovered regulatory mechanisms governing cellular fitness and gene expression.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-06-20T08:55:47.576Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3sdsc83vsn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3sdsc83vsn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mei-sheng","last_name":"Xiao","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Arun Prasath","last_name":"Damodaran","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bandana","last_name":"Kumari","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ethan","last_name":"Dickson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kun","last_name":"Xing","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tyler","last_name":"On","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nikhil","last_name":"Parab","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Helen E. ","last_name":"King","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alexendar R.","last_name":"Perez","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wilfried M. ","last_name":"Guiblet","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gerard","last_name":"Duncan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Anney","last_name":"Che","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Raj","last_name":"Chari","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thorkell","last_name":"Andresson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Joana A.","last_name":"Vidigal","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Robert J.","last_name":"Weatheritt","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Michael","last_name":"Aregger","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thomas","last_name":"Gonatopoulos-Pournatzis","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Microscopy"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":133288,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":151,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":133288,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":132565,"restricted":68,"embargoed":655},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2253},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":672},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":469},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":419},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":415},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":403},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":396},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":331},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":326},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":267}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":130660},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1900},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":185},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":131},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":76},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":66},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":56},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":37},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":32},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":27}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":511},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":407},{"id":"f58d7a83-6efa-5d8a-a6c2-b9e78ee14783","name":"Maharishi Markandeshwar Institute of Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation","count":356},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":354},{"id":"9d63ad1d-c391-5c35-a12e-cafe17017098","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid","count":308}]}}